  "Question": "Each of the \\(39\\) students in the eighth grade at Lincoln Middle School has one dog or one cat or both a dog and a cat. Twenty students have a dog and \\(26\\) students have a cat. How many students have both a dog and a cat?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( \\ 7 \\)",
    "B": "\\( \\ 13 \\)",
    "C": "\\( \\ 19 \\)",
    "D": "\\( \\ 39 \\)",
    "E": "\\( \\ 46 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Adding the dog owners and cat owners gives \\(20+26=46\\). Every student is included because each has at least one of the two pets. A student with just one pet is counted once, while a student with both pets is counted twice.\n\nThus the amount by which \\(46\\) exceeds the actual number of students counts the students with both pets exactly once:\n\\[\n46-39=7.\n\\]\nTherefore \\(7\\) students have both a dog and a cat, choice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).",
